-- Query: eb_summary_period (DR4 names)
-- Serves: Question C. Number of eclipsing binaries per quarter-decade of period (log10 of the period in days, lower
--   edge).
-- Names: the draft DR4 data model of 26 Jun 2026. The schema name gaiadr4 is taken from that model's own example
--   query.
-- DR3 stand-in: dr3/eb_summary_period.adql, made from this file by make_standin.py. DR3 tables:
--   gaiadr3.vari_eclipsing_binary.
-- Last ran without error on the DR3 stand-in: 2026-10-27 (15 rows; results/run_log.tsv).
-- Last ran on DR4: never. The archive has no DR4 until 2 Dec 2026.
-- DR4 columns this query relies on:
--   gaiadr4.vari_eclipsing_binary: frequency
-- Lines tagged DR4ONLY have no DR3 equivalent and are dropped from the stand-in.
-- Cannot be tested before release: The DR4 period distribution, in particular the longest periods DR4 reports (ESA
--   states no maximum).
SELECT
    t.log_period_bin,
    COUNT(*) AS n_sources
FROM (
    SELECT FLOOR(LOG10(1.0 / eb.frequency) * 4.0) / 4.0 AS log_period_bin
    FROM gaiadr4.vari_eclipsing_binary AS eb
    WHERE eb.frequency > 0.0
) AS t
GROUP BY t.log_period_bin
ORDER BY t.log_period_bin
